#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""swarm-handoff: ask a person to take over the browser (docs/design/live-browser.md §4.1).

    swarm-handoff request --reason "Sign in to GitHub as the bot account" --expect github.com
    swarm-handoff wait [REQUEST_ID]
    swarm-handoff status
    swarm-handoff device PRESET
    swarm-handoff theme dark|light|system
    swarm-handoff record start NAME [--interval-ms N]
    swarm-handoff record stop
    swarm-handoff serve DIR [--port N]

It WRITES FILES and opens no socket: a request goes into the spool at
$SWARM_HANDOFF (`requests/<id>.json`, written to a temporary name and renamed),
and the worker beside the agent -- which holds the attempt key and the gate's
channel -- answers in `responses/<id>.json`. The same reasons as the child-task
spool: no new listener in the agent's reach, and a request survives a
checkpoint. The worker's half is `agent_worker.handoff`; the exit codes below
are restated from it and a unit test holds them equal.

`wait` blocks until the hand-off is resolved, for at most 9 minutes per call,
because claude-code's Bash tool kills a command at 10 (#736). It reads the
worker's answer every POLL_SECONDS and never faster than MIN_POLL_SECONDS,
whatever `--poll` says: the helper is never the busy loop. Every answer it
prints carries `next`, what the agent should do now -- above all, on 0 and
75, NOT to poll the browser: measured on task_2ac5d7e22a51460995a2, an agent
ran `curl /json/version` in a loop after `wait` returned (HANDOFF-POLICY).
Exits:

     0  control was returned; a JSON summary is on stdout
    75  still waiting: call `wait` again
     3  the wait expired; the worker is checkpointing and parking
     4  the task is being cancelled
     5  refused (rate limit, no live path, reason invalid)

FLOW GIFS (QA-FLOWS, owner decision 2026-10-19, part of #1649). `record start`
launches a recorder in the background, detached from the agent's shell, and
returns; `record stop` asks it to stop and prints what it wrote. The recorder
connects to the live browser over CDP ($SWARM_CDP_ENDPOINT, under the image's
venv Python, which carries Playwright) and screenshots the page on screen
after every main-frame navigation and every --interval-ms (default 1000,
bounded to 250..10000). An input that changes the page is in the next tick's
frame: another client's CDP input is not visible to this one, and the gate,
which sees it, is not this command's to change. A frame like the last is not
a frame -- the last is shown longer -- and only the rows that changed are
encoded again. The frames become $SWARM_ARTIFACTS_DIR/flows/<name>.gif, which
is a whole GIF after every frame (the trailer is rewritten), so a recorder
killed between frames still leaves one.

What a flow costs, and its caps. The image carries NO image library (its
Dockerfile installs Playwright and Chromium, nothing that writes a GIF), so
the encoder below is the standard library's: zlib to read Chromium's PNG,
LZW written here. Frames are taken by the page's own screenshot at CSS size
and fitted to at most MAX_FRAME_WIDTH x MAX_FRAME_HEIGHT (a 1440x900 desktop
becomes 720x450, a 390x844 phone stays as it is), and coloured from a fixed
216-colour cube with no dithering: a flow is evidence of what happened, the
PNG screenshots are the fidelity. The recorder takes the screenshot through
the session its own connection already holds for the page, never a CDP
session of its own: the gate refuses a second browser session, and the first
QA run recorded nothing for it (QA-002, QA-TOOLS-FIX). So the 1440x900 PNG is
decoded here, not one Chromium had already halved. MEASURED 2026-10-20
(QA-TOOLS-FIX, Python 3.11, one core, FlowGif.add_png on a synthetic
1440x900 RGBA PNG): 0.08 s of CPU filtered Up, 0.15 s and 433 KB for
unfiltered random noise, and 1.61 s all-Paeth, the worst case (it was 0.29 s
when Chromium returned 720x450) -- a UI page is tens of KB, and a frame that
changed a few rows is that band only. That CPU is the
agent container's (requests == limits), which is why the interval has a
floor; a frame waits for the one before it, never piles up. A flow stops itself at MAX_FLOW_FRAMES frames,
MAX_FLOW_BYTES bytes (before the frame that would pass it; under the 20 MiB
the console draws inline) or MAX_FLOW_SECONDS, and says which. A frame is
never shown for more than MAX_FRAME_DELAY_CS, so an idle minute plays as two
seconds. While a person is in control the gate holds the recorder's CDP like
the agent's, and a screenshot that completes in that window is withheld
(cdppolicy.CONTENT_METHODS), so no frame shows what a person typed.

A MOCKUP BESIDE THE APP. `serve DIR` serves a directory over http on
127.0.0.1 and nowhere else -- there is no option for another address -- in
the background, and prints its URL; the live Chromium opens it in a tab of
its own (file:// is blocked by chromium-policy.json). The display sidecar
shares the pod's network namespace, as the gate's CDP proxy on 127.0.0.1:9222
does with the agent, and Chromium sends loopback direct even when its egress
is proxied (the bypass list never says `<-loopback>`). Only GET and HEAD, only
inside DIR (a link out of it is not followed), and only for a Host of
127.0.0.1 or localhost -- a site in the same browser that rebinds its own name
to 127.0.0.1 is refused, as the CDP proxy refuses it.

Standard library only: this runs in the agent's environment, under any Python
the image carries. The recorder alone needs Playwright, and runs under the
venv's Python, which has it.
"""

import argparse
import http.server
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import signal
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import zlib
from pathlib import Path

EXIT_RETURNED = 0
EXIT_EXPIRED = 3
EXIT_CANCELLED = 4
EXIT_REFUSED = 5
EXIT_STILL_WAITING = 75

#: Under claude-code's 10-minute Bash limit, with a minute to spare.
WAIT_SECONDS = 9 * 60
#: A device switch is answered on the worker's next poll (10 s).
DEVICE_WAIT_SECONDS = 30
#: The colour schemes `theme` takes (QA-KIT): `agent_worker.livegate.presets.THEMES`,
#: restated because this runs under any Python the image carries; a unit test
#: holds them equal. `system` lifts the override.
THEMES = ("dark", "light", "system")
POLL_SECONDS = 0.5
#: The floor under `--poll`: a file read every 100 ms is not a busy loop.
MIN_POLL_SECONDS = 0.1
MAX_REASON_CHARS = 200
FINAL = {"returned", "expired", "cancelled", "refused", "unavailable", "applied"}

#: QA-FLOWS (module docstring): where a flow lands under the task's artifacts,
#: and what a flow may be called -- a file name, never a path.
FLOWS_DIR_NAME = "flows"
FLOW_NAME = re.compile(r"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,47}")
#: The caps (module docstring says what each costs). 200 frames at the default
#: interval is over three minutes of activity; 8 MiB is a GIF a report can
#: carry and the console draws inline (Artifacts.tsx: up to 20 MiB).
MAX_FLOW_FRAMES = 200
MAX_FLOW_BYTES = 8 * 1024 * 1024
MAX_FLOW_SECONDS = 15 * 60
FLOW_INTERVAL_MS = 1000
MIN_INTERVAL_MS = 250
MAX_INTERVAL_MS = 10000
#: A frame's size: half of a 1440 desktop, a phone at its own width.
MAX_FRAME_WIDTH = 720
MAX_FRAME_HEIGHT = 900
#: The longest a frame is shown for, in GIF's hundredths of a second.
MAX_FRAME_DELAY_CS = 200
#: The spool's record of the one running recorder, the stop it is asked by,
#: what it wrote, and its stderr.
RECORDING_NAME = "recording.json"
RECORDING_STOP = "recording.stop"
RECORDING_RESULT = "recording-result.json"
RECORDING_LOG = "recording.log"
#: How long `record stop` waits for the recorder to finish its frame.
STOP_WAIT_SECONDS = 30
#: The Python that carries Playwright on the browser image (claude_code.VENV_BIN).
VENV_PYTHON = "/opt/venv/bin/python"
#: A screenshot that takes longer than this is skipped, not waited on: the
#: gate holds every CDP command while a person is in control.
CAPTURE_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000

FRAME_ADDED = "added"
FRAME_SAME = "same"
STOP_ASKED = "stopped"
STOP_FRAME_CAP = "frame_cap"
STOP_SIZE_CAP = "size_cap"
STOP_TIME_CAP = "time_cap"

#: `serve`'s one address. A mockup is for the browser in this pod, nobody else.
SERVE_HOST = "127.0.0.1"


#: What the agent should do on each exit of `wait`, printed as `next`.
NEXT = {
    # LB-RETURN: MEASURED on 4+ acceptance runs, the agent's read after a
    # return came back empty -- it read the first tab, or a value from before.
    EXIT_RETURNED: (
        "Control is back, and the person may have changed the page: read it FRESH, "
        "once. Do not reuse a page handle, snapshot or value from before the hand-off. "
        "From Python: connect again (`playwright, browser, context = live()`) and take "
        "`swarm_browser.handoff_page(context)` -- the tab at this `url`, not "
        "`context.pages[0]`. With the browser_* tools: browser_tabs, select the tab at "
        "this `url`, then browser_snapshot. Then carry on with the task; do not poll the "
        "browser or CDP in a loop."
    ),
    EXIT_STILL_WAITING: (
        "Someone may still come. Run `swarm-handoff wait` again now, in the "
        "foreground; do not poll the browser or CDP meanwhile -- it is paused "
        "for the person."
    ),
    EXIT_EXPIRED: (
        "Nobody came in time. Write where you stopped into $SWARM_HANDOFF/notes.md "
        "now and stop; the task is parked until a person is ready."
    ),
    EXIT_CANCELLED: "The task is being cancelled. Stop now.",
    EXIT_REFUSED: "Refused. Carry on without help, or fail with this reason.",
}


def _out(document):
    sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(document) + "\n")
    sys.stdout.flush()


def _refuse(code, message):
    _out({"outcome": "refused", "code": code, "message": message, "next": NEXT[EXIT_REFUSED]})
    return EXIT_REFUSED


def _spool():
    value = os.environ.get("SWARM_HANDOFF", "")
    if not value:
        return None
    root = Path(value)
    return root if root.is_dir() else None


def _unavailable(root):
    """The worker's marker: this attempt has no live path, and why."""
    marker = root / "unavailable"
    if not marker.exists():
        return None
    try:
        data = json.loads(marker.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        return str(data.get("code") or "unavailable")
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return "unavailable"


def _write_atomic(path, document):
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = path.with_name(path.stem + ".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(document), encoding="utf-8")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def _read(path):
    try:
        data = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else None


def _await(root, request_id, seconds, poll):
    """The worker's final answer for `request_id`, or None after `seconds`."""
    path = root / "responses" / (request_id + ".json")
    deadline = time.monotonic() + seconds
    poll = max(MIN_POLL_SECONDS, poll)
    while True:
        answer = _read(path)
        if answer is not None and answer.get("outcome") in FINAL:
            return answer
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            return None
        time.sleep(poll)


def _exit_for(answer):
    code = answer.get("exit")
    if isinstance(code, int) and code in (EXIT_RETURNED, EXIT_EXPIRED, EXIT_CANCELLED, EXIT_REFUSED):
        return code
    return EXIT_REFUSED


def cmd_request(args, root):
    reason = (args.reason or "").strip()
    if not reason:
        return _refuse("reason_invalid", "--reason is required: say what the person is asked to do")
    if len(reason) > MAX_REASON_CHARS:
        return _refuse("reason_invalid", "--reason is at most %d characters" % MAX_REASON_CHARS)
    why = _unavailable(root)
    if why:
        return _refuse(why, "this attempt has no live browser path; carry on without help")
    request_id = args.id or ("h-" + secrets.token_hex(6))
    document = {"reason": reason}
    if args.expect:
        document["expect"] = args.expect.strip().lower()
    _write_atomic(root / "requests" / (request_id + ".json"), document)
    (root / ".last").write_text(request_id, encoding="utf-8")
    _out({"request_id": request_id, "outcome": "requested"})
    return EXIT_RETURNED


def cmd_wait(args, root):
    request_id = args.request_id
    if not request_id:
        try:
            request_id = (root / ".last").read_text(encoding="utf-8").strip()
        except OSError:
            request_id = ""
    if not request_id:
        return _refuse("no_request", "nothing to wait for: run `swarm-handoff request` first")
    answer = _await(root, request_id, args.max_seconds, args.poll)
    if answer is None:
        _out({"request_id": request_id, "outcome": "waiting",
              "next": NEXT[EXIT_STILL_WAITING]})
        return EXIT_STILL_WAITING
    code = _exit_for(answer)
    _out({**answer, "next": NEXT[code]})
    return code


def cmd_status(args, root):
    answer = _read(root / "status.json")
    _out(answer if answer is not None else {"outcome": "none"})
    return EXIT_RETURNED


def cmd_device(args, root):
    why = _unavailable(root)
    if why:
        return _refuse(why, "this attempt has no live browser path")
    request_id = "d-" + secrets.token_hex(6)
    _write_atomic(root / "devices" / (request_id + ".json"), {"preset": args.preset})
    answer = _await(root, request_id, args.max_seconds, args.poll)
    if answer is None:
        return _refuse("no_answer", "the worker did not answer the device switch")
    _out(answer)
    return EXIT_RETURNED if answer.get("outcome") == "applied" else EXIT_REFUSED


def cmd_theme(args, root):
    why = _unavailable(root)
    if why:
        return _refuse(why, "this attempt has no live browser path")
    request_id = "t-" + secrets.token_hex(6)
    _write_atomic(root / "themes" / (request_id + ".json"), {"theme": args.theme})
    answer = _await(root, request_id, args.max_seconds, args.poll)
    if answer is None:
        return _refuse("no_answer", "the worker did not answer the theme change")
    _out(answer)
    return EXIT_RETURNED if answer.get("outcome") == "applied" else EXIT_REFUSED


# -- flow GIFs (QA-FLOWS) -------------------------------------------------------

_PNG_SIGNATURE = b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n"


def _unfilter(kind, line, prev, bpp):
    """One PNG scanline with its filter undone (PNG spec §9)."""
    if kind == 0:
        return bytes(line)
    if kind == 2:
        # Bytewise (a + b) mod 256 over the whole row at once, as one integer
        # with the carries kept inside each byte.
        n = len(line)
        a = int.from_bytes(line, "big")
        b = int.from_bytes(prev, "big")
        low = int.from_bytes(b"\x7f" * n, "big")
        high = int.from_bytes(b"\x80" * n, "big")
        return (((a & low) + (b & low)) ^ ((a ^ b) & high)).to_bytes(n, "big")
    row = bytearray(line)
    n = len(row)
    if kind == 1:
        for i in range(bpp, n):
            row[i] = (row[i] + row[i - bpp]) & 0xFF
    elif kind == 3:
        for i in range(n):
            left = row[i - bpp] if i >= bpp else 0
            row[i] = (row[i] + ((left + prev[i]) >> 1)) & 0xFF
    elif kind == 4:
        for i in range(n):
            a = row[i - bpp] if i >= bpp else 0
            b = prev[i]
            c = prev[i - bpp] if i >= bpp else 0
            p = a + b - c
            pa, pb, pc = abs(p - a), abs(p - b), abs(p - c)
            row[i] = (row[i] + (a if pa <= pb and pa <= pc else b if pb <= pc else c)) & 0xFF
    else:
        raise ValueError("not a PNG filter: %d" % kind)
    return bytes(row)


def decode_png(data):
    """`(width, height, channels, pixels)` of an 8-bit RGB or RGBA PNG, what
    Chromium's `Page.captureScreenshot` writes. Anything else is a ValueError."""
    if not data.startswith(_PNG_SIGNATURE):
        raise ValueError("not a PNG")
    pos = len(_PNG_SIGNATURE)
    header = None
    idat = []
    while pos + 8 <= len(data):
        length, kind = struct.unpack(">I4s", data[pos:pos + 8])
        body = data[pos + 8:pos + 8 + length]
        pos += 12 + length
        if kind == b"IHDR":
            header = struct.unpack(">IIBBBBB", body)
        elif kind == b"IDAT":
            idat.append(body)
        elif kind == b"IEND":
            break
    if header is None:
        raise ValueError("a PNG with no header")
    width, height, depth, colour, _compression, _filter, interlace = header
    if depth != 8 or colour not in (2, 6) or interlace:
        raise ValueError("only 8-bit, non-interlaced RGB or RGBA")
    if not 0 < width <= 16384 or not 0 < height <= 16384:
        raise ValueError("a PNG of an impossible size")
    channels = 3 if colour == 2 else 4
    stride = width * channels
    raw = zlib.decompress(b"".join(idat))
    if len(raw) != height * (stride + 1):
        raise ValueError("a PNG whose data is not its size")
    prev = bytes(stride)
    rows = []
    for y in range(height):
        at = y * (stride + 1)
        prev = _unfilter(raw[at], raw[at + 1:at + 1 + stride], prev, channels)
        rows.append(prev)
    return width, height, channels, b"".join(rows)


#: The palette: a 6x6x6 colour cube, padded to 256 (unused) entries. Index
#: 36r + 6g + b is the colour (51r, 51g, 51b), so a pixel is quantised by
#: three byte translations and one sum, all in C.
_LEVEL = bytes(min(5, (v + 25) // 51) for v in range(256))
_TO_R = bytes(36 * _LEVEL[v] for v in range(256))
_TO_G = bytes(6 * _LEVEL[v] for v in range(256))
PALETTE = b"".join(bytes((51 * (i // 36), 51 * (i // 6 % 6), 51 * (i % 6))) for i in range(216)) + bytes(3 * 40)
WHITE = 215


def quantise(pixels, channels):
    """One palette index per pixel."""
    r = pixels[0::channels].translate(_TO_R)
    g = pixels[1::channels].translate(_TO_G)
    b = pixels[2::channels].translate(_LEVEL)
    n = len(r)
    # Never above 180 + 30 + 5 = 215, so no byte carries into the next.
    return (int.from_bytes(r, "big") + int.from_bytes(g, "big") + int.from_bytes(b, "big")).to_bytes(n, "big")


def _fit(indices, width, height, canvas_width, canvas_height):
    """`indices` shrunk by a whole step until it fits the canvas, then padded
    with white to the canvas's size: a device switch mid-flow."""
    step = max(1, -(-width // canvas_width), -(-height // canvas_height))
    rows = [indices[y * width:(y + 1) * width:step] for y in range(0, height, step)][:canvas_height]
    pad = bytes([WHITE])
    out = [row[:canvas_width] + pad * (canvas_width - len(row[:canvas_width])) for row in rows]
    out += [pad * canvas_width] * (canvas_height - len(out))
    return b"".join(out)


def lzw(indices):
    """GIF's variable-length LZW (GIF89a appendix F) over 8-bit indices."""
    clear, end = 256, 257
    out = bytearray()
    acc = bits = 0
    size, nxt = 9, 258
    table = {}

    def emit(code):
        nonlocal acc, bits
        acc |= code << bits
        bits += size
        while bits >= 8:
            out.append(acc & 0xFF)
            acc >>= 8
            bits -= 8

    emit(clear)
    prefix = indices[0]
    for byte in indices[1:]:
        key = (prefix << 8) | byte
        code = table.get(key)
        if code is not None:
            prefix = code
            continue
        emit(prefix)
        if nxt < 4095:
            table[key] = nxt
            nxt += 1
            if nxt > (1 << size) and size < 12:
                size += 1
        else:
            emit(clear)
            table.clear()
            size, nxt = 9, 258
        prefix = byte
    emit(prefix)
    emit(end)
    if bits:
        out.append(acc & 0xFF)
    return bytes(out)


def _sub_blocks(data):
    return b"".join(bytes([len(data[i:i + 255])]) + data[i:i + 255] for i in range(0, len(data), 255)) + b"\x00"


class FlowGif:
    """A GIF written frame by frame, whole on disk after every frame."""

    def __init__(self, path, *, max_frames=MAX_FLOW_FRAMES, max_bytes=MAX_FLOW_BYTES,
                 max_width=MAX_FRAME_WIDTH, max_height=MAX_FRAME_HEIGHT):
        self.path = Path(path)
        self.max_frames = max_frames
        self.max_bytes = max_bytes
        self.max_width = max_width
        self.max_height = max_height
        self.frames = 0
        self.size = 0
        self.stopped = None
        self._file = None
        self._canvas = None
        self._width = self._height = 0
        self._shown_at = None
        self._delay_at = None

    def add_png(self, png, *, at):
        """Add one screenshot, taken at `at` (seconds). FRAME_ADDED, FRAME_SAME,
        or the cap that stops the flow -- then nothing more is added."""
        if self.stopped:
            return self.stopped
        if self.frames >= self.max_frames:
            self.stopped = STOP_FRAME_CAP
            return self.stopped
        width, height, channels, pixels = decode_png(png)
        indices = quantise(pixels, channels)
        if self._canvas is None:
            step = max(1, -(-width // self.max_width), -(-height // self.max_height))
            self._width, self._height = -(-width // step), -(-height // step)
        frame = _fit(indices, width, height, self._width, self._height)
        if frame == self._canvas:
            return FRAME_SAME
        top, bottom = 0, self._height
        if self._canvas is not None:
            w = self._width
            while frame[top * w:(top + 1) * w] == self._canvas[top * w:(top + 1) * w]:
                top += 1
            while frame[(bottom - 1) * w:bottom * w] == self._canvas[(bottom - 1) * w:bottom * w]:
                bottom -= 1
        band = frame[top * self._width:bottom * self._width]
        block = (b"\x21\xF9\x04\x04" + struct.pack("<H", MAX_FRAME_DELAY_CS) + b"\x00\x00"
                 + b"\x2C" + struct.pack("<HHHHB", 0, top, self._width, bottom - top, 0)
                 + b"\x08" + _sub_blocks(lzw(band)))
        if self._file is None:
            head = (b"GIF89a" + struct.pack("<HHBBB", self._width, self._height, 0xF7, WHITE, 0) + PALETTE
                    + b"\x21\xFF\x0BNETSCAPE2.0\x03\x01\x00\x00\x00")
            if len(head) + len(block) + 1 > self.max_bytes:
                self.stopped = STOP_SIZE_CAP
                return self.stopped
            self.path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            self._file = open(self.path, "w+b")
            self._file.write(head + b";")
            self.size = len(head) + 1
        elif self.size + len(block) > self.max_bytes:
            self.stopped = STOP_SIZE_CAP
            return self.stopped
        self._hold(at)
        self._file.seek(self.size - 1)
        self._delay_at = self.size - 1 + 4
        self._file.write(block + b";")
        self._file.flush()
        self.size += len(block)
        self.frames += 1
        self._canvas = frame
        self._shown_at = at
        return FRAME_ADDED

    def _hold(self, at):
        """Set the last frame's delay to the time until `at`, under the cap."""
        if self._delay_at is None or self._shown_at is None:
            return
        delay = max(1, min(MAX_FRAME_DELAY_CS, int(round((at - self._shown_at) * 100))))
        self._file.seek(self._delay_at)
        self._file.write(struct.pack("<H", delay))

    def close(self, *, at):
        if self._file is not None:
            self._hold(at)
            self._file.close()
            self._file = None
        return {"path": str(self.path), "frames": self.frames, "bytes": self.size,
                "stopped": self.stopped or STOP_ASKED}


class LiveFrames:
    """Screenshots of the page on screen in the live browser, over CDP.

    One connection for the whole flow, through the gate's CDP proxy like the
    agent's own; a lost one is opened again on the next tick. The page on
    screen is the one whose document is visible; with none, the page that
    navigated last.
    """

    def __init__(self, endpoint):
        self.endpoint = endpoint
        self._playwright = None
        self._context = None
        self._last = None
        self._navigated = False

    def _connect(self):
        if self._context is not None:
            return self._context
        from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright

        playwright = sync_playwright().start()
        try:
            browser = playwright.chromium.connect_over_cdp(self.endpoint, timeout=CAPTURE_TIMEOUT_MS)
            context = browser.contexts[0] if browser.contexts else None
        except Exception:
            playwright.stop()
            raise
        if context is None:
            playwright.stop()
            raise RuntimeError("the live browser has no context")
        self._playwright, self._context = playwright, context
        context.on("page", self._watch)
        for page in context.pages:
            self._watch(page)
        return context

    def _watch(self, page):
        def navigated(frame):
            if frame == page.main_frame:
                self._last = page
                self._navigated = True

        page.on("framenavigated", navigated)

    def _on_screen(self, pages):
        for page in reversed(pages):
            try:
                if page.evaluate("() => document.visibilityState") == "visible":
                    return page
            except Exception:
                continue
        if self._last in pages:
            return self._last
        return pages[-1] if pages else None

    def capture(self):
        try:
            context = self._connect()
            page = self._on_screen(list(context.pages))
            if page is None:
                return None
            # The page's own screenshot, on the session this connection's
            # Playwright already holds for the page -- the path the agent's
            # browser_take_screenshot takes. NEVER `context.new_cdp_session`:
            # that asks for a browser session of the recorder's own
            # (`Target.attachToBrowserTarget`), which the gate refuses
            # (cdppolicy.DENIED: "a second browser session is the proxy's to
            # open"), and every frame of the first QA run was skipped for it
            # (QA-002). CSS size; FlowGif fits it to MAX_FRAME_WIDTH x
            # MAX_FRAME_HEIGHT. caret="initial" and animations="allow" leave
            # the person's page as it is: the defaults would inject a style.
            return page.screenshot(type="png", scale="css", caret="initial", animations="allow",
                                   timeout=CAPTURE_TIMEOUT_MS)
        except Exception as exc:
            sys.stderr.write("frame skipped: %s\n" % type(exc).__name__)
            self.close()
            return None

    def wait(self, seconds):
        """Wait `seconds`, or less when a page navigates -- its frame is next."""
        deadline = time.monotonic() + seconds
        self._navigated = False
        while time.monotonic() < deadline and not self._navigated:
            pages = list(self._context.pages) if self._context is not None else []
            try:
                if pages:
                    pages[-1].wait_for_timeout(min(100, max(1, (deadline - time.monotonic()) * 1000)))
                else:
                    time.sleep(min(0.1, max(0.0, deadline - time.monotonic())))
            except Exception:
                time.sleep(min(0.1, max(0.0, deadline - time.monotonic())))
        if self._navigated and self._last is not None:
            try:
                self._last.wait_for_load_state("load", timeout=3000)
            except Exception:
                pass

    def close(self):
        playwright, self._playwright, self._context = self._playwright, None, None
        if playwright is not None:
            try:
                playwright.stop()
            except Exception:
                pass


def record_loop(frames, flow, *, stop_file, interval, max_seconds=MAX_FLOW_SECONDS, clock=time.monotonic):
    """Frames into `flow` until the stop file, a cap, or `max_seconds`."""
    started = clock()
    stopped = None
    try:
        while True:
            if Path(stop_file).exists():
                break
            if clock() - started >= max_seconds:
                stopped = STOP_TIME_CAP
                break
            png = frames.capture()
            if png is not None:
                try:
                    outcome = flow.add_png(png, at=clock())
                except ValueError as exc:
                    sys.stderr.write("frame skipped: %s\n" % exc)
                    outcome = None
                if outcome in (STOP_FRAME_CAP, STOP_SIZE_CAP):
                    break
            frames.wait(interval)
    finally:
        frames.close()
        result = flow.close(at=clock())
    if stopped:
        result["stopped"] = stopped
    return result


def _alive(pid):
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        return True
    return True


def _recording(root):
    state = _read(root / RECORDING_NAME)
    if state is None or not isinstance(state.get("pid"), int):
        return None
    return state


def cmd_record(args, root):
    if args.action == "_run":
        return _record_run(args, root)
    if args.action == "stop":
        return _record_stop(root)
    name = args.name or ""
    if not FLOW_NAME.fullmatch(name):
        return _refuse("name_invalid", "a flow is named in lower-case letters, digits and dashes, "
                                       "at most 48 (it becomes flows/<name>.gif)")
    endpoint = os.environ.get("SWARM_CDP_ENDPOINT", "").strip()
    artifacts = os.environ.get("SWARM_ARTIFACTS_DIR", "").strip()
    why = _unavailable(root)
    if why or not endpoint or not artifacts:
        return _refuse(why or "no_live_path", "this attempt has no live browser to record")
    state = _recording(root)
    if state is not None and _alive(state["pid"]):
        return _refuse("already_recording", "%s is being recorded: run `swarm-handoff record stop` first"
                       % state.get("name"))
    interval = max(MIN_INTERVAL_MS, min(MAX_INTERVAL_MS, int(args.interval_ms)))
    path = Path(artifacts) / FLOWS_DIR_NAME / (name + ".gif")
    for stale in (RECORDING_STOP, RECORDING_RESULT):
        (root / stale).unlink(missing_ok=True)
    python = VENV_PYTHON if os.path.exists(VENV_PYTHON) else sys.executable
    with open(root / RECORDING_LOG, "ab") as log:
        proc = subprocess.Popen(
            [python, os.path.abspath(__file__), "record", "_run", name, "--interval-ms", str(interval)],
            stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=log, stderr=log, start_new_session=True, close_fds=True)
    _write_atomic(root / RECORDING_NAME, {"name": name, "pid": proc.pid, "path": str(path),
                                          "interval_ms": interval})
    _out({"outcome": "recording", "name": name, "path": str(path), "interval_ms": interval,
          "max_frames": MAX_FLOW_FRAMES, "max_bytes": MAX_FLOW_BYTES, "max_seconds": MAX_FLOW_SECONDS,
          "next": "Do the flow, then run `swarm-handoff record stop`."})
    return EXIT_RETURNED


def _record_run(args, root):
    """The recorder itself, in the background (`record start` launched it)."""
    state = _recording(root) or {}
    artifacts = os.environ.get("SWARM_ARTIFACTS_DIR", "").strip()
    path = Path(state.get("path") or Path(artifacts) / FLOWS_DIR_NAME / (args.name + ".gif"))
    stop_file = root / RECORDING_STOP

    def on_term(_signum, _frame):
        stop_file.write_text("", encoding="utf-8")

    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, on_term)
    frames = LiveFrames(os.environ.get("SWARM_CDP_ENDPOINT", "").strip())
    result = record_loop(frames, FlowGif(path), stop_file=stop_file, interval=args.interval_ms / 1000.0)
    _write_atomic(root / RECORDING_RESULT, result)
    return EXIT_RETURNED


def _record_stop(root):
    state = _recording(root)
    if state is None:
        return _refuse("not_recording", "nothing is being recorded: run `swarm-handoff record start <name>`")
    (root / RECORDING_STOP).write_text("", encoding="utf-8")
    deadline = time.monotonic() + STOP_WAIT_SECONDS
    result = None
    while True:
        result = _read(root / RECORDING_RESULT)
        if result is not None or not _alive(state["pid"]) or time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            break
        time.sleep(POLL_SECONDS)
    if result is None and _alive(state["pid"]):
        try:
            os.kill(state["pid"], signal.SIGTERM)
        except OSError:
            pass
    (root / RECORDING_NAME).unlink(missing_ok=True)
    if result is None:
        path = Path(state.get("path") or "")
        written = path.is_file()
        _out({"outcome": "recorded" if written else "failed", "name": state.get("name"),
              "path": str(path), "bytes": path.stat().st_size if written else 0,
              "log": str(root / RECORDING_LOG)})
        return EXIT_RETURNED if written else EXIT_REFUSED
    _out({"outcome": "recorded", "name": state.get("name"), **result})
    return EXIT_RETURNED


# -- a mockup beside the app (QA-FLOWS) -------------------------------------------


class _MockupHandler(http.server.SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):
    """GET and HEAD inside one directory, for a loopback Host only."""

    def _refused(self):
        host = (self.headers.get("Host") or "").strip().lower()
        port = self.server.server_address[1]
        return host not in {"127.0.0.1", "localhost", "127.0.0.1:%d" % port, "localhost:%d" % port}

    def send_head(self):
        if self._refused():
            self.send_error(403, "only http://127.0.0.1:<port>/ is served")
            return None
        path = Path(self.translate_path(self.path))
        root = Path(self.directory).resolve()
        try:
            resolved = path.resolve()
        except OSError:
            resolved = None
        if resolved is None or (resolved != root and root not in resolved.parents):
            self.send_error(404, "not inside the served directory")
            return None
        return super().send_head()

    def log_message(self, format, *args):
        pass


def mockup_server(directory, port, host=SERVE_HOST):
    """The server `serve` runs, bound to 127.0.0.1 and nothing else."""
    if host != SERVE_HOST:
        raise ValueError("a mockup is served on %s only" % SERVE_HOST)
    directory = str(Path(directory).resolve())

    def handler(*a, **k):
        return _MockupHandler(*a, directory=directory, **k)

    return http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer((SERVE_HOST, port), handler)


def cmd_serve(args):
    directory = Path(args.directory)
    if not directory.is_dir():
        return _refuse("not_a_directory", "%s is not a directory" % args.directory)
    try:
        server = mockup_server(directory, args.port)
    except OSError as exc:
        return _refuse("port_unavailable", "cannot listen on %s:%d (%s)" % (SERVE_HOST, args.port, exc.strerror))
    port = server.server_address[1]
    pid = os.fork()
    if pid:
        server.socket.close()
        _out({"outcome": "serving", "url": "http://%s:%d/" % (SERVE_HOST, port), "pid": pid,
              "directory": str(directory.resolve()),
              "next": "Open the url in a new tab of the live browser (browser_tabs new, then browser_navigate); "
                      "`kill %d` stops it." % pid})
        return EXIT_RETURNED
    # The child: no terminal, no pipe of the agent's shell held open.
    os.setsid()
    devnull = os.open(os.devnull, os.O_RDWR)
    for fd in (0, 1, 2):
        os.dup2(devnull, fd)
    try:
        server.serve_forever()
    finally:
        os._exit(0)


def build_parser():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="swarm-handoff", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest="command", required=True)
    request = sub.add_parser("request", help="ask a person to take over the browser")
    request.add_argument("--reason", required=True)
    request.add_argument("--expect", help="the bare host the person should sign in on")
    request.add_argument("--id", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    wait = sub.add_parser("wait", help="wait for the person (at most 9 minutes)")
    wait.add_argument("request_id", nargs="?")
    wait.add_argument("--max-seconds", type=float, default=WAIT_SECONDS, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    wait.add_argument("--poll", type=float, default=POLL_SECONDS, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    sub.add_parser("status", help="the last control episode")
    device = sub.add_parser("device", help="switch the browser to a device preset by name")
    device.add_argument("preset")
    device.add_argument("--max-seconds", type=float, default=DEVICE_WAIT_SECONDS, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    device.add_argument("--poll", type=float, default=POLL_SECONDS, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    theme = sub.add_parser("theme", help="set the colour scheme pages are told to prefer")
    theme.add_argument("theme", choices=THEMES)
    theme.add_argument("--max-seconds", type=float, default=DEVICE_WAIT_SECONDS, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    theme.add_argument("--poll", type=float, default=POLL_SECONDS, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    record = sub.add_parser("record", help="record a flow as $SWARM_ARTIFACTS_DIR/flows/<name>.gif")
    record.add_argument("action", choices=("start", "stop", "_run"))
    record.add_argument("name", nargs="?")
    record.add_argument("--interval-ms", type=int, default=FLOW_INTERVAL_MS,
                        help="a frame at least this often (%d..%d)" % (MIN_INTERVAL_MS, MAX_INTERVAL_MS))
    serve = sub.add_parser("serve", help="serve a directory on http://127.0.0.1:<port>/ for the live browser")
    serve.add_argument("directory")
    serve.add_argument("--port", type=int, default=0, help="a port (default: any free one)")
    return parser


def main(argv=None):
    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)
    if args.command == "wait":
        args.max_seconds = max(0.0, min(args.max_seconds, WAIT_SECONDS))
    if args.command == "serve":
        return cmd_serve(args)
    root = _spool()
    if root is None:
        return _refuse("no_live_path", "this task has no live browser ($SWARM_HANDOFF is not set)")
    handler = {"request": cmd_request, "wait": cmd_wait, "status": cmd_status, "device": cmd_device,
               "theme": cmd_theme, "record": cmd_record}
    return handler[args.command](args, root)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
